IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`
IMPORT `g9-sched1-commissioner`
IMPORT `g9-sched2-tribunal`

-- g9-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT to fail, and are counted. Each is the discriminating case of one fork, asserted with the answer of the OTHER reading against the favoured interpretation (reading A
-- of every fork). The other reading's answer is tested, and holds, in the module that tests that reading (g9-tests-periods.l4, g9-tests-sched1.l4, g9-tests-sched2.l4), where it is asked of the other reading.
-- This module therefore proves two things: that the harness (check.sh) can see a failed assertion, and that each fork changes the answer on its discriminating case: if an assertion here ever passed, the fork would have no discriminating case.
-- One assertion per fork point: 19 in all (F9.1 to F9.19), so the number of failed assertions that check.sh expects of this module is 19.

`A` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
`no earlier service` MEANS EMPTY

-- F9.1: appointment on 15 March 2026, notice on 1 March: reading B says it is late; reading A says it is in time
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
-- F9.2: a term from 1 March 2026 to 1 March 2032: reading B says it is over 6 years; reading A says it is within the limit
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1) 6
-- F9.3: notice given on 30 November 2026 for 28 February 2027: reading B says the office ended on the day the notice was given; reading A on 28 February 2027
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day the office ends by resignation` `A` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 2 28) 3 EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 11 30)
-- F9.4: absent from 1 to 29 March 2026: reading B counts 28 elapsed days, not longer than 4 weeks; reading A counts 29 days
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 29) 4
-- F9.5: terminated on 1 March 2026, notice on 15 March: reading B says it is late; reading A says it is in time
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of a termination was presented in time` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
-- F9.6: service from 1 March 2026: reading B completes 12 years on 26 February 2038 (4,380 days); reading A on 1 March 2038
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `A` `no earlier service` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 2 26
-- F9.7: a report on 2026 provided on 1 May 2027: reading B says it is in time (31 December plus 4 months rolled is 1 May); reading A says it is late
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` `A` 2026 (YMD 2027 5 1) 4
-- F9.8: staff deregister an entity on its own application: reading B says staff may (only the refusal is reserved); reading A says they may not
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 4(3) a member of the Commissioner's staff may exercise the function on behalf of the Commissioner` `A` (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`) TRUE
-- F9.9: in the text of 16 December 2019 with an Order directing the cost to the Fund: reading B says the remuneration must still be paid out of the annual income of the States; reading A says it need not
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(4)(a) the remuneration of the Commissioner must be paid out of the annual income of the States` `A` `the text of 16 December 2019` TRUE
-- F9.10: the copy laid 42 days after receipt, the judgement being that it was as soon as practicable: reading B (28 days) says it was not; reading A takes the judgement
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` `A` TRUE (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 3 15)
-- F9.11: a 14 month spell as a designated relevant person before an appointment from 1 June 2027: reading B counts it and completes 12 years on 1 April 2038; reading A on 1 June 2039
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `A` (LIST `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2027 5 1), TRUE) (YMD 2027 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 4 1
-- F9.12: the office held from 1 November 2026 to 30 June 2027: reading B requires no report for 2026; reading A requires one
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `A` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2026
-- F9.13: 24 months from 1 March 2027 is 731 days: reading B says it is over the cap of 730 days; reading A says 24 months is within the cap
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `A` (`Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`) (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- F9.14: views sought on the day of the appointment: reading B says that is before appointing; reading A says it is not
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15)
-- F9.15: the office of chair vacant and the vice-chair at the sitting: reading B says the Law does not answer; reading A says the vice-chair presides
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `A` `the office is vacant` `at the sitting`
-- F9.16: the decision on entry in the restricted section: reading B says it is reserved from staff; reading A says it is not
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` `A` (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`)
GIVEN member IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
`build an appointment red` member MEANS
    `Appointment of the Commissioner` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2032 3 1), TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, (JUST member), `no earlier service`
-- F9.17: a person already a member of the States when appointed: reading B ends the appointment on its first day; reading A finds no such day
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(4)(b) the day the person becomes a member of the States` `A` (`build an appointment red` (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- F9.18: two members of staff available, Dee named by the Minister: reading B makes both of them the responsible officer; reading A makes Dee alone
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3(2) the members of staff who are the responsible officer` `A` (LIST "Dee", "Eli") (JUST "Dee") EQUALS LIST "Dee", "Eli"
-- F9.19: absent 28 days (not longer than 4 weeks), the Minister satisfied: reading B finds the ground made out; reading A does not
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has been absent for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` `A` (`Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)), (JUST (YMD 2026 3 28)), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
